[system]
You keep the continuity bible for a novelist. You record only what the scene's own words state. You never guess, infer or add.
[user]
WHO AND WHAT (use these ids as "subject")
{% for e in entities %}
- {{ e.id }} = {{ e.name }}{% if e.aliases %} (also: {{ e.aliases | join(", ") }}){% endif %}

{% endfor %}
{% if secrets %}

THINGS NOT EVERYONE KNOWS (for "mentions_fact")
{% for label, about in secrets %}
- {{ label }}{% if about != label %}: {{ about }}{% endif %}

{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

SCENE {{ scene_id }}{% if when %} (story date: {{ when }}){% endif %}

"""{{ text }}"""

List up to {{ max_facts }} facts this scene states about the people, places and things above.
For each fact:
- "subject": one id from the list.
- "predicate": what kind of fact (allowed values below).
- "value": the fact itself, short. For a person, place or thing, write its id.
- "quote": copy 4–25 words exactly as they appear in the scene that state this fact.

Predicates:
- eye_color, hair, height, handedness, title_rank, age — a person's lasting details ("value": grey / left / constable / 34).
- status — alive, dead or injured.
- location_at — the person is physically in this place now ("value": a location id).
- active — the person speaks or acts in this scene in person ("value": what they do, 2–6 words).
- has_item — the person holds or uses a thing ("value": an item id).
- held_by — a thing changes hands; subject is the item ("value": the id of who has it now).
- located_at — where a thing is kept; subject is the item ("value": a location id).
- condition — a thing is intact, broken, lost or destroyed; subject is the item.
- date_of_event — a date written in the scene for a letter, document or event ("value": YYYY-MM-DD).
{% if secrets %}
- mentions_fact — the person shows they know one of the THINGS NOT EVERYONE KNOWS ("value": that line's label, before the colon).
{% endif %}

Skip anything the scene does not state in words. An empty list is a correct answer.

Example of the expected shape (different story):
{"facts": [{"subject": "char-anna", "predicate": "eye_color", "value": "brown", "quote": "Anna's brown eyes narrowed at the open ledger"},
  {"subject": "obj-lantern", "predicate": "held_by", "value": "char-anna", "quote": "He pressed the lantern into Anna's hands"}]}
